@host = http://localhost:4004
@t3 = f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@T3 = {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets({{t3}})/TicketService

# ==========================================================
#  A. CHECK THE SEED DATA (run first)
# ==========================================================

### A1. All tickets (expect 4: T-2026-000001 to T-2026-000004)
GET {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets

### A2. T3 details (expect status New, priority P1, no assigned agent)
GET {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets({{t3}})

### A3. T3 SLA clocks (expect FIRST_RESPONSE and RESOLUTION, both Running)
GET {{host}}/tickets/SLAClocks?$filter=ticket_ID eq {{t3}}


# ==========================================================
#  B. VALIDATIONS ON A NEW TICKET (T3)
# ==========================================================

### B1. Resolve while status is New (expect 409)
POST {{T3}}.resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resolutionNote": "Too early" }

### B2. Start work before assigning (expect 409)
POST {{T3}}.startWork
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### B3. Change status directly (expect 400)
PATCH {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets({{t3}})
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Closed" }

### B4. Assign a Sales user (expect 400: only a Service agent)
POST {{T3}}.assign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "agent": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003" }

### B5. Assign an agent that doesn't exist (expect 404)
POST {{T3}}.assign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "agent": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099" }


# ==========================================================
#  C. FULL LIFECYCLE ON T3 (run in order, one time per restart)
# ==========================================================

### C1. Assign to the Service agent (expect status Assigned)
POST {{T3}}.assign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "agent": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001" }

### C2. Accept
POST {{T3}}.accept
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C3. Start work (expect status In Progress)
POST {{T3}}.startWork
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C4. Agent emails the customer (FIRST_RESPONSE clock should stop)
POST {{host}}/tickets/Interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ticket_ID": "{{t3}}",
  "type": "Email",
  "message": "We are checking the outage. Please confirm which services are down.",
  "author_ID": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"
}

### C5. Clocks (FIRST_RESPONSE: stoppedAt filled, status Met or Breached)
GET {{host}}/tickets/SLAClocks?$filter=ticket_ID eq {{t3}}

### C6. Wait for customer (RESOLUTION clock becomes Paused, pausedAt set)
POST {{T3}}.waitForCustomer
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C7. Clocks (RESOLUTION: status Paused)
GET {{host}}/tickets/SLAClocks?$filter=ticket_ID eq {{t3}}

### C8. Customer replied (RESOLUTION back to Running, dueAt pushed later, totalPausedMins updated)
POST {{T3}}.customerReplied
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C9. Clocks again
GET {{host}}/tickets/SLAClocks?$filter=ticket_ID eq {{t3}}

### C10. Escalate without a reason (expect 400)
POST {{T3}}.escalate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "agent": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002" }

### C11. Escalate to a non-lead agent (expect 400: must be Team Lead or Manager)
POST {{T3}}.escalate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "agent": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003", "reason": "Wrong target" }

### C12. Escalate to the Team Lead
POST {{T3}}.escalate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "agent": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "reason": "Needs L2 network expert" }

### C13. Assignment history (expect Assign, Accept, Escalate)
GET {{host}}/tickets/TicketAssignments?$filter=ticket_ID eq {{t3}}

### C14. Resolve without a note (expect 400)
POST {{T3}}.resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resolutionNote": "" }

### C15. Resolve (expect status Resolved, RESOLUTION clock stopped)
POST {{T3}}.resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resolutionNote": "Core switch replaced, services restored." }

### C16. Close before resolving is not possible now, so close after resolve (expect status Closed)
POST {{T3}}.close
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C17. Reopen (expect status Reopened, new RESOLUTION clock)
POST {{T3}}.reopen
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C18. Final check: ticket, interactions, clocks
GET {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets({{t3}})

###
GET {{host}}/tickets/Interactions?$filter=ticket_ID eq {{t3}}

###
GET {{host}}/tickets/SLAClocks?$filter=ticket_ID eq {{t3}}


# ==========================================================
#  D. TICKET T4: RESUME A PAUSED CLOCK (seed: Waiting for Customer)
# ==========================================================

### D1. T4 clocks (expect RESOLUTION Paused)
GET {{host}}/tickets/SLAClocks?$filter=ticket_ID eq f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004

### D2. Customer replied on T4 (expect status In Progress, clock Running)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets(f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004)/TicketService.customerReplied
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### D3. T4 clocks again
GET {{host}}/tickets/SLAClocks?$filter=ticket_ID eq f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004


# ==========================================================
#  E. TICKET T2: WARRANTY CHECK AND SALES HAND-OVER (seed: In Progress)
# ==========================================================

### E1. Warranty check (expect underWarranty true, warrantyEndDate 2027-06-01)
GET {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets(f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)/TicketService.checkWarranty()

### E2. Warranty check on a ticket without product/order (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets(f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003)/TicketService.checkWarranty()

### E3. Raise opportunity with a Service user as owner (expect 400: must be Sales)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets(f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)/TicketService.raiseOpportunity
Content-Type: application/json

{ "owner": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001", "expectedValue": 20000 }

### E4. Raise opportunity (expect 200 with opportunityID)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets(f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)/TicketService.raiseOpportunity
Content-Type: application/json

{ "owner": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003", "expectedValue": 20000 }

### E5. Raise it again (expect 409: already has an open opportunity)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets(f1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002)/TicketService.raiseOpportunity
Content-Type: application/json

{ "owner": "d1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003", "expectedValue": 20000 }


# ==========================================================
#  F. CREATE A NEW TICKET (independent, does not feed other requests)
# ==========================================================

### F1. Create ticket (expect 201, ticketNo T-2026-000005, status New, priority P2)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "contact_ID":  "c2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "category_ID": "b2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "title": "Slow internet in branch office",
  "description": "Speed drops after 5 PM"
}

### F2. Contact that doesn't exist (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "contact_ID":  "c2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099",
  "category_ID": "b2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "title": "x"
}

### F3. Contact of another customer (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "contact_ID":  "c2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "category_ID": "b2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "title": "x"
}

### F4. Missing title (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/tickets/ServiceTickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "c1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "contact_ID":  "c2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "category_ID": "b2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "title": ""
}